  message: "Cross-item review 2026-05-17: forms a --gzip-coherence pair with WI-mokim. This item: producer side (--gzip writes gzipped binary to a non-.gz path silently). WI-mokim: consumer side (11 cli.py --input subcommands plus four scripts don't accept .gz). The two failure modes compose: a user who avoids this item's pitfall by adding .gz to --out still hits WI-mokim when feeding the output back into compact/slice/io-boundaries/etc. Both reference the original WI-kojob --gzip introduction. Consider landing together (or document the partial state in release notes) so users don't have an arc where producer is fixed but consumer remains broken."  # 3851
